0d467-caec-5c0d-8ad6-c8bce8cc4b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-3742" :question/is-example false :question/problem "$4-\\frac{(-2)}{q}=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $4=\\frac{4}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{1}-\\frac{(-2)}{q}=.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $q$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{1}-\\frac{(-2)}{q} & = \\\\ \\frac{q}{q}\\cdot \\frac{4}{1}-\\frac{(-2)}{q} & = \\\\ \\frac{4q}{q}-\\frac{(-2)}{q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4q}{q}-\\frac{(-2)}{q} & = \\\\ \\frac{4q-(-2)}{q} & = \\\\ \\frac{4q+2}{q} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(2q+1)}{q}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3742/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63080bb8-7a6a-505d-813a-e6c99d337064"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69903/selection/b2abecb122ed2a10730ead2815b26e4a374b46e3fae0c9214e6caa32e4b31734" :answer/id #uuid "53ebc276-de74-53da-81c4-fb98ee52ac80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{x(1+z)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69903/selection/aee30c17e78b82b158b699909de11447039f7627a590f0fee7e53c64471ee215" :answer/id #uuid "b50a07a4-88b1-555a-82dc-c234238ef7df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{6(1+z)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69903/selection/e79735303399b5cc5685f6813043e3aece8e04e4f9aadb10e27a8b912fb0ce27" :answer/id #uuid "b2862fef-0a01-5f96-b4b6-334165c988d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3-x}{3x(1+z)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69903/selection/eaf9809dda2300d2f40f9c4d4870a57733ee0a2c5d1a3263cedb24a13af1e481" :answer/id #uuid "d